Because we're such a high-volume customer;-)  ACPI has been promoted out
from under Power Management, up to its own top-level category on
kernel.org bugzilla.  Underneath ACPI are 12 sub-components, split
between configuration, power-management, and issues specific to the AML
interpreter itself:

AML-Interpreter
Config-Interrupts
Config-Procesors
Config-Tables
Config-Tables
Power-Battery
Power-Fan
Power-Off
Power-Procesor
Power-Sleep-Wake
Power-Thermal
Power-Other

The default owners for each comoponent are virtual accounts.
"you can watch any bug's changes that are owned by these accounts by
setting up your 'Users to watch' in Email Settings of your bugzilla
preferences.

We'll set up acpi-bugzilla-5NWGOfrQmneRv+LV9MX5urNAH6kLmebB@public.gmane.org to watch all of them; and
will continue adding that alias to the cc-list for acpi bugs for when
they're owned by somebody else.  If you'd like to get acpi-related
bugzilla e-mail, sign up here:

http://lists.sourceforge.net/lists/listinfo/acpi-bugzilla

If you'd like to just see when new bugs are created and assigned to the
virtual accounts, then watch the owners listed here:

http://bugzilla.kernel.org/describecomponents.cgi?product=ACPI

cheers,
-Len

ps. old PM/ACPI component will be deleted when all the bugs have been
categorized into the new name space.




